2.1 Version-controlled change log
Version 1.0 is the approved baseline. Version 1.1 contains the approved changes.
CR ID	Req. ID	Old Requirement	New Requirement	Reason	Status
CR-01	SAFE-01	Enter Safe Mode when critical battery or thermal condition is detected.	Enter Safe Mode within 3 seconds when chamber or battery temperature exceeds its critical threshold, or battery capacity falls below the emergency level.	Defines exact triggers and a measurable time limit.	Modified
CR-02	NFR-02	Support communication with multiple robots simultaneously.	Support at least 20 simultaneously connected robots.	Defines a measurable capacity for the pilot.	Modified
CR-03	FR-09	Only authenticated operators may issue robot commands.	Authenticate the operator and verify role-based authorisation before accepting any robot command.	Clearly specifies both authentication and authorisation.	Modified
2.2 Why the new requirements are more testable
- CR-01: A tester can simulate each critical condition and measure whether Safe Mode starts within 3 seconds.
- CR-02: A tester can connect 20 robots simultaneously and check whether all remain connected and communicate correctly.
- CR-03: A tester can use valid, invalid, and insufficiently privileged accounts to verify that commands are accepted or rejected correctly.
